  <div class="plate" id="m-t0">
    <h3>Inside t0-gamma: a causal patch transformer that also attends across covariates</h3>
    <p>t0-gamma (The Forecasting Company, October 2026, 256M parameters, Apache-2.0) reads the history of the target, of past-only covariates and of covariates known into the future, and returns 21 quantiles for every forecast step. Like TimesFM it reads time left to right; like Chronos-2 it has a second kind of attention that runs across the variates of one series. Step through it below. Sources: Meyer et al., <a class="text-primary-600 hover:underline" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.24559">t0: A Time-Series Foundation Model for Forecasting with Context</a> (technical report, September 2026, which describes t0-alpha and t0-beta in detail), the <a class="text-primary-600 hover:underline" href="https://huggingface.co/theforecastingcompany/t0-gamma">t0-gamma model card</a> and <a class="text-primary-600 hover:underline" href="https://www.theforecastingcompany.com/blog/t0-gamma/">release post</a> (“a similar architecture to t0-beta”), and the official inference code, <a class="text-primary-600 hover:underline" href="https://github.com/theforecastingcompany/tfc-t0">tfc-t0</a>. There is no separate report for gamma, so every size below was read from gamma's released <code>config.json</code> and weight file, and the table at the end says where each claim comes from.</p>
    <div class="ctrl"><div class="seg" id="t0Step"><button aria-pressed="true" data-v="0">Whole network</button><button aria-pressed="false" data-v="1">1 · Scale</button><button aria-pressed="false" data-v="2">2 · Patch</button><button aria-pressed="false" data-v="3">3 · Embed</button><button aria-pressed="false" data-v="4">4 · 24 layers</button><button aria-pressed="false" data-v="5">5 · Decode</button></div></div>
    <div class="fig wide" id="figT0arch"></div>
    <p class="stepcap" id="t0Cap"></p>

