    <h3 class="mt-4">What is stated, what we checked, and what is not published</h3>
    <div class="tw">
      <table class="mtable">
        <thead><tr><th>Claim</th><th>Status for t0-gamma</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Width 1,024, 24 layers in the pattern time-time-variate, 8 heads, SwiGLU 2,048, patch 32, 21 quantile levels, arcsinh scaling</td><td><b>checked</b>: <code>config.json</code> and the weight shapes; also the model card's architecture table</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Causal scaling, role embeddings, time attention causal for y and x and bidirectional for z, variate attention where z is read but does not read back, next-patch decoder, monotone quantiles</td><td><b>stated</b> in the report for t0-alpha (§4.1) and <b>checked</b> in the tfc-t0 code that loads gamma's weights (<code>mask.py</code>, <code>patch_encoder.py</code>, <code>head.py</code>)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Horizon appended as blanked patches and decoded in one pass up to 1,024 steps; rollout beyond</td><td><b>stated</b> in the report (§4.3) and the model card, <b>checked</b> in <code>rollout.py</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Training: next-patch quantile loss at every patch boundary, contiguous patch masking (TiRex), 2-D packing, curriculum from univariate to multivariate data</td><td><b>stated for t0-alpha only</b>. The report's alpha uses 5 quantile levels; gamma's weights have 21, so its loss must differ. Gamma's data, steps and loss weights are <b>not published</b>; treat them as unknown</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Benchmark scores</td><td>self-reported. The model card gives GIFT-Eval CRPS 0.4503, the release post 0.4520 (the post says its numbers are recomputed with each leaderboard's method)</td></tr>
